.TH "DAHARNESS\-PG" "1" "" "daharness 0.1.0" "daharness manual"
.SH NAME
daharness\-pg \(em provision the optional engagement\-cobweb Postgres
lane
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]daharness\-pg\f[R] \f[I]init\f[R] | \f[I]start\f[R] |
\f[I]stop\f[R] | \f[I]status\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The deb ships the engagement journal/evidence lane with its Postgres
drivers wired but no server: out of the box the lane is silently off and
the SQLite stores carry the journal.
When a Postgres\-backed cobweb is wanted, \f[B]daharness\-pg\f[R] (run
via \f[I]sudo\f[R]) provisions a \f[B]dedicated cluster\f[R] named
\f[CR]daharness\f[R] on \f[B]port 5433\f[R] with
\f[B]pg_createcluster\f[R].
It never touches msfdb\(aqs \f[CR]main\f[R] cluster on 5432 \(em in
either direction: an msfdb re\-init cannot drop the harness database,
and the harness cluster cannot collide with msf\(aqs port.
.PP
\f[CR]daharness\-pg init\f[R]:
.IP \(bu 2
verifies the Postgres server tooling exists
(\f[CR]pg_createcluster\f[R], \f[CR]pg_ctlcluster\f[R], \f[CR]psql\f[R],
\f[CR]createdb\f[R]); absent tooling prints the exact \f[B]apt install
postgresql\f[R] remediation and changes nothing;
.IP \(bu 2
creates and starts the dedicated cluster (autostart, so it returns after
reboots via \f[I]postgresql.service\f[R]);
.IP \(bu 2
creates the \f[CR]harness\f[R] database;
.IP \(bu 2
runs the shipped init bundle (roles + password ALTERs, schemas, SECURITY
DEFINER \f[CR]engagement.purge()\f[R], operator registry ACL) from
\f[CR]/usr/share/daharness/postgres/init/\f[R] with
\f[CR]\-v ON_ERROR_STOP=1\f[R];
.IP \(bu 2
writes resolved knobs to \f[CR]/etc/daharness/pg.env\f[R]
(HARNESS_DB_HOST/PORT/NAME plus one
HARNESS_DB_PASSWORD_{OPERATOR,BRAIN,GATEWAY,REPL} per lane role), mode
0640 root:daharness \(em the systemd units read it via a tolerant
\f[CR]EnvironmentFile=\-\f[R] line, and an operator shell sources it
before running the REPL.
.PP
\f[CR]init\f[R] is idempotent: it reuses lane passwords already recorded
in pg.env, re\-runs the bundle (roles are IF NOT EXISTS;
schemas/functions are CREATE IF NOT EXISTS) and rewrites pg.env from
live state.
Lane passwords are 128\-bit random hex minted at first init;
\f[B]rotate\f[R] by moving pg.env aside, re\-running \f[CR]init\f[R],
and restarting the daharness units.
.PP
Without the lane, \f[CR]utils/engagement.py\f[R] degrades honestly (it
logs once that Postgres is unavailable and journals stay on SQLite);
lane role and host selection honor the HARNESS_DB_* environment knobs
documented in \f[I]daharness.env\f[R](5).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
\f[B]init\f[R] \(em provision or repair the lane; requires root.
.PP
\f[B]start\f[R] / \f[B]stop\f[R] \(em start/stop the dedicated cluster
(\f[I]pg_ctlcluster\f[R]; requires root).
.PP
\f[B]status\f[R] \(em cluster presence, readiness on 127.0.0.1:5433, and
whether pg.env is in place.
Works as any user.
.SH FILES
\f[CR]/etc/daharness/pg.env\f[R] \(em generated lane knobs (not a
package conffile: it is operator data and survives upgrades and
\f[I]\-\-purge\f[R]).
.PP
\f[CR]/usr/share/daharness/postgres/init/001_roles.sh\f[R],
\f[CR]002_schemas.sql\f[R], \f[CR]003_functions.sql\f[R],
\f[CR]004_operator_registry_acl.sql\f[R] \(em shipped init bundle.
